; joystick.txt -- copy into the game directory (beside bdg.txt) to choose devices. Optional: without it the
; first stick SDL lists supplies everything, as before. The game reads the log lines "[joy] device n: ..." at
; start; copy a name or a guid from there.
;
; primary: the device that supplies buttons, the hat and (by default) the axes
; primary = Logitech Extreme 3D
;
; axis <slot> = <device> a<k>: slot reads axis k of that device. Slots: 0 roll, 1 pitch, 2 rudder, 3 throttle,
; 4 and 5 spare. A device is a guid (32 hex digits) or a name (exact, else part of it); add #2 for the second
; of two identical devices. Indexes are never used: SDL renumbers devices when a USB port changes.
; axis 2 = Pedals a2
; axis 3 = 030000006d04000015c2000010010000 #1 a3
